      "dcDescription": [
        "Handkolorerat vykort. 0092.0002 Fire-breathing dancers. This 1906 postcard reproduced from a photograph by O. E. Meddaugh shows men painted, costumed, and ready for ceremonies that were rarely witnessed even then. Each man (tentatively identified) assumes a role for the Upper Lake roundhouse performance that is said to be religious in nature: (from left to right) Jim Rickabaugh, Johnny Bull (a fire eater and chief of Shigom), Dick Green (Whiskey Head), \"Snap\" Bucknell (best dancer), and Charles Rickabaugh (a fire eater). (Courtesy Lake County Historic Courthouse Museum). (Patrick, K. C., 2008,"
      ],
